---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { BRAND, CONTACT_EMAIL, DEMO_URL } from '../lib/constants';

const updated = '12 November 2026';
---

<!--
  TEMPLATE — NEEDS LEGAL REVIEW BEFORE LAUNCH.
  This page is a plain-language description of what the code does today. It has not been
  reviewed by a lawyer and is not tailored to any jurisdiction (GDPR, UK GDPR, CCPA, …).
  Before launch: name the legal entity, add a real contact address (CONTACT_EMAIL in
  src/lib/constants.ts), name the email provider behind WAITLIST_WEBHOOK, and confirm
  retention periods.
-->
<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy — BluePainter"
  description="What the BluePainter site and Studio demo collect, where it goes, and what stays in your browser."
>
  <section class="section prose">
    <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p class="muted">Last updated {updated}</p>
    <p>
      {BRAND.name} is a validation prototype. We collect as little as we can. This page describes what this
      website and the Studio demo at <a href={DEMO_URL}>{DEMO_URL.replace(/^https?:\/\//, '')}</a> actually do.
    </p>

    <h2>What the forms collect</h2>
    <p>The newsletter form, the pilot request form and the “email me the report” fields on the free tools collect:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Email address</strong> — required.</li>
      <li><strong>Name, company or team, role and a message</strong> — optional, pilot form only.</li>
      <li><strong>Which form you used</strong> (for example “newsletter” or “pilot”).</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      We use this only to contact you about the newsletter or a pilot. We do not sell it or share it for
      advertising.
    </p>

    <h2>Where it goes</h2>
    <p>
      Submissions are sent to a small serverless function that runs with this site on Vercel. That function
      forwards the entry to the email tool we use to manage the waitlist. Ask us at any time and we will
      delete your entry.
    </p>

    <h2>The free tools</h2>
    <p>
      The contrast checker, receipt grader and TSX id analyzer run entirely in your browser. The colours,
      values and code you paste are not sent to us. Only the email address is sent, and only if you choose
      to submit it.
    </p>

    <h2>Shared scorecards</h2>
    <p>
      A scorecard link from the Studio carries its numbers in the part of the URL after the <code>#</code>.
      Browsers do not send that part to servers, so we do not receive or store it. Anyone you give the link
      to can see those numbers.
    </p>

    <h2>The Studio demo</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Browser storage.</strong> The Studio keeps your workspace, receipt policy settings,
        feedback notes and session history in your browser's <code>localStorage</code>. It stays on your
        device until you clear it or export it yourself.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Tokens you enter.</strong> If you enter a GitHub, Vercel, Figma or OpenAI token in the
        Studio, it is sent to the Studio's own serverless functions only so they can call GitHub, Vercel,
        Figma or OpenAI on your behalf for the action you asked for. The token is kept in your browser —
        for the current tab only, or in <code>localStorage</code> if you tick “Remember”. Use tokens with
        the narrowest scope that works, and revoke them when you are done.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Content you send to those services.</strong> When you push, deploy, import or generate copy,
        the relevant code or text is sent to that service and is covered by its own privacy policy.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Analytics, cookies and fonts</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        We use Vercel Web Analytics to count page views. It does not use cookies and does not build a
        profile of you across sites.
      </li>
      <li>This site sets no advertising or tracking cookies.</li>
      <li>Fonts are loaded from Google Fonts, so your browser makes a request to Google when a page loads.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Your choices</h2>
    <p>
      You can ask us to show you, correct or delete anything you submitted through a form, and you can
      unsubscribe from email at any time.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>Questions or requests: <strong>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</strong></p>

    <p class="stack-lg"><a href="/terms">Terms →</a></p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
